    "question": "Sienna gave Bailey half of her suckers. Jen ate half and gave the rest to Molly. Molly ate 2 and gave the rest to Harmony. Harmony kept 3 and passed the remainder to Taylor. Taylor ate one and gave the last 5 to Callie. How many suckers did Jen eat?",
    "gold": "11",
    "answer": "Taylor received 5 + 1 = <<5+1=6>>6 suckers.\nHarmony was given 3 + 6 = <<3+6=9>>9 suckers.\nMolly received 9 + 2 = <<9+2=11>>11 suckers from Jen.\nJen originally had 11 * 2 = <<11*2=22>>22 suckers.\nJen ate 22 – 11 = <<22-11=11>>11 suckers.\n#### 11"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "Let's denote the total number of suckers Sienna originally had as \\( x \\).\n\n1. Sienna gave Bailey half of her suckers. So, Bailey received \\( \\frac{x}{2} \\) suckers.\n2. Jen ate half of the suckers she received from Sienna, which is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{x}{2} = \\frac{x}{4} \\). Jen then gave the rest to Molly, which is \\( \\frac{x}{2} - \\frac{x}{4} = \\frac{x}{4} \\).\n3. Molly ate 2 suckers and gave the rest to Harmony. So, Harmony received \\( \\frac{x}{4} - 2 \\) suckers.\n4. Harmony kept 3 suckers and passed the remainder to Taylor. So, Taylor received \\( \\frac{x}{4} - 2 - 3 = \\frac{x}{4} - 5 \\) suckers.\n5. Taylor ate one sucker and gave the last 5 suckers to Callie. So, Taylor received 5 suckers from Callie, which means \\( \\frac{x}{4} - 5 = 5 \\). Solving for \\( x \\), we get \\( \\frac{x}{4} = 10 \\), so \\( x = 40 \\).\n\nNow, we need to find out how many suckers Jen ate. Jen ate half of the suckers she received from Sienna, which is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{40}{2} = \\frac{40}{4} = 10 \\).\n\nTherefore, the number of suckers Jen ate is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
